    title: "前 OpenAI 員工涉嫌在辦公室植入隱藏錄音設備竊聽機密會議",
    summary: "美國司法部（DoJ）宣布，一名前 OpenAI 員工 Abdulrahman Alfozan 被捕，涉嫌在公司舊金山辦公室的高階會議室植入隱藏錄音設備，以竊聽公司關於「超級智慧」（super intelligence）技術的敏感對話。根據指控，該設備於 2026 年 9 月 30 日左右被發現，植入於會議室電視的 USB 連接埠內，並被偽裝在衛生紙中。指控指出，該會議室用於討論高度機密的技術、商業和戰略資訊，包括專有研究和產品計畫。FBI 稱，保護美國的 AI 創新是國家安全和經濟穩定的關鍵任務。此外，指控還提到 Alfozan 曾利用未指明的生產力工具收集公司地址和會議資訊，甚至利用其配偶的聊天機器人帳號提交了關於建構、客製化和遠端存取錄音設備的提示。OpenAI 表示，他們已將此事交予 FBI 處理，並強調其安全計畫能應對從內部風險到國家級威脅的各種威脅。若定罪，Alfozan 面臨最高 5 年監禁和 $250,000 的罰款。",
    tags: ["OpenAI", "Abdulrahman Alfozan", "竊聽", "內部威脅", "國家安全", "超級智慧"],
    title_en: "Former OpenAI Employee Allegedly Planted Hidden Recording Device in Office to Eavesdrop on Confidential Meetings",
    summary_en: "The U.S. Department of Justice (DoJ) announced the arrest of former OpenAI employee Abdulrahman Alfozan, who is suspected of planting hidden recording devices in the company's San Francisco office to eavesdrop on sensitive discussions regarding 'super intelligence' technology. According to the charges, the device was discovered around September 30, 2026, planted within a USB port on a conference room television and disguised as toilet paper. The charges state that the conference room was used to discuss highly confidential technical, commercial, and strategic information, including proprietary research and product plans. The FBI stated that protecting American AI innovation is a critical mission for national security and economic stability. Furthermore, the charges mention that Alfozan utilized unspecified productivity tools to gather company addresses and meeting information, and even used his spouse's chatbot account to submit prompts concerning the construction, customization, and remote access of recording equipment. OpenAI stated that it has handed the matter over to the FBI and emphasized that its security protocols are capable of addressing various threats, from internal risks to national-level threats. If convicted, Alfozan faces a maximum of 5 years in prison and a $250,000 fine.",
