    summary_en: "Canonical engineer Juerg Haefliger released a set of Device Tree patches designed to enable the main Linux kernel to support the HP EliteBook 6 G1q laptop equipped with the Qualcomm Snapdragon X1 Plus SoC. While there has been recent work enabling Linux for Snapdragon X2 hardware, support remains lacking for laptops in the X1 Plus class. These patches optimize support for the EliteBook 6 G1q (chipset: Snapdragon X1P42100), bringing its functionality close to that of the already supported HP OmniBook X14. With these patches, the main kernel has confirmed good support for most major functionalities, including the keyboard, touchpad, screen, USB A/C, Ethernet card, HDMI-A, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, built-in audio, camera, fingerprint reader, and WWAN modem. The article notes that patches for the eDP display panel and the WWAN modem will be released separately, and hopes these patches will quickly enter the main kernel tree.",
