    summary_en: "KDE Plasma 6.8 has been officially released, a feature-rich and heavily optimized desktop environment. This release is particularly significant as it marks the 30th anniversary of the KDE project. This update brings several exciting improvements, including vRAM usage optimization, support for dwell clicker in Wayland environments, KWin support for the Wayland commit-timing protocol, enhanced Union theme engine, improved remote desktop support, improved multi-GPU capabilities, and the addition of the kscreenctl tool. Specifically regarding Wayland, Plasma 6.8 features extensive polishing and fine-tuning, significantly improving overall multi-display and multi-monitor support. Users can visit KDE.org for the full release announcement to learn more details.",
