    trackers: ["os", "security"],
    category: "Linux",
    title: "Linux 核心修復 UDP 長度溢位漏洞：限制 PMTU 發現時的 MTU 處理",
    summary: "本漏洞存在於 Linux 核心的網路堆疊中，涉及 IPv4 協定。當網路設備的 MTU（最大傳輸單元）設定超過 IP_MAX_MTU，且使用者設定 `setsockopt IP_MTU_DISCOVER` 為 `IP_PMTUDISC_PROBE` 時，若傳送一個大型封包，可能導致 UDP 長度計算發生溢位（overflow）。此漏洞的根本原因是 `cork->base.fragsize` 的設定沒有被限制在 `IP_MAX_MTU`，使得 UDP 長度欄位計算時超出 16 位元限制，觸發警告（WARN）。修復措施是將 `cork->base.fragsize` 限制為 `IP_MAX_MTU`，以防止此類溢位。此修復主要影響處理 PMTU 發現的 IPv4 網路路徑。開發者應確保使用已修補的 Linux 核心版本，以避免潛在的網路服務不穩定性。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "IPv4", "UDP", "MTU", "PMTUDISC_PROBE", "cork"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Fixes UDP Length Overflow Vulnerability: MTU Handling When Limiting PMTU Discovery",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability resides in the Linux kernel's network stack, involving the IPv4 protocol. When a network device's MTU (Maximum Transmission Unit) is set above IP_MAX_MTU, and a user sets `setsockopt IP_MTU_DISCOVER` to `IP_PMTUDISC_PROBE`, sending a large packet can cause an overflow in the UDP length calculation. The root cause of this vulnerability is that `cork->base.fragsize` is not restricted to `IP_MAX_MTU`, causing the UDP length field calculation to exceed the 16-bit limit, which triggers a warning (WARN). The fix involves restricting `cork->base.fragsize` to `IP_MAX_MTU` to prevent such overflows. This fix primarily affects IPv4 network paths handling PMTU discovery. Developers should ensure they use a patched Linux kernel version to avoid potential network service instability.",
    tags_en: ["Linux Kernel", "IPv4", "UDP", "MTU", "PMTUDISC_PROBE", "cork"],
    sources: [
      { name: "NVD CVE API", url: "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98393", lang: "EN" }
    ]
