    category: "Linux",
    title: "Linux 核心 Wi-Fi 驅動程式存在堆疊緩衝區溢出漏洞，影響 key 移除操作",
    summary: "本漏洞位於 Linux 核心的 Wi-Fi 相關程式碼中，具體影響是 `wifi: rsi` 驅動程式在移除加密金鑰（key removal）時，執行 `rsi_hal_load_key()` 函式。當金鑰被移除（`data == NULL`）時，程式會執行 `memset` 操作。然而，由於計算錯誤，`memset` 寫入的資料偏移量超出了預期的 160 位元組 `skb` 資料緩衝區，導致寫入操作（OOB write）污染了堆積記憶體中不相關的物件。此漏洞會在每次執行 `DISABLE_KEY` 回呼時觸發，包括正常的斷線、漫遊或介面關閉等操作。開發者 Atuin 發現了此問題，並已在核心中修復。修補建議是移除冗餘的 `memset` 呼叫，因為整個緩衝區在分配後已經被清零，移除該程式碼分支不會影響正常操作。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "wifi", "rsi", "heap OOB write", "CVE-2026-98407"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Wi-Fi Driver Contains Stack Buffer Overflow Vulnerability Affecting Key Removal Operation",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability resides in the Wi-Fi related code within the Linux kernel. Specifically, the `wifi: rsi` driver executes the `rsi_hal_load_key()` function when removing an encryption key (key removal). When the key is removed (`data == NULL`), the program performs a `memset` operation. However, due to a calculation error, the offset written by `memset` exceeds the expected 160-byte `skb` data buffer, leading to an Out-of-Bounds (OOB) write that contaminates unrelated objects in the stack memory. This vulnerability is triggered every time the `DISABLE_KEY` callback is executed, including normal operations such as disconnection, roaming, or interface shutdown. The issue was discovered by developer Atuin and has been patched in the kernel. The suggested fix is to remove the redundant `memset` call, as the entire buffer is already zeroed after allocation, and removing this code branch does not affect normal operation.",
    tags_en: ["Linux Kernel", "wifi", "rsi", "heap OOB write", "CVE-2026-98407"],
    sources: [
      { name: "NVD CVE API", url: "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98407", lang: "EN" }
    ]
