    summary: "本篇公告指出在 Linux 核心中發現了一個 watchdog: rzv2h 的漏洞。該漏洞的根本問題在於 clk_get_rate() 函式可能回傳 0，若未經適當處理，將導致系統執行除零操作，進而引發系統崩潰（panic）。此修補旨在確保在 clk_get_rate() 可能回傳 0 的情況下，系統能夠安全地避免除零錯誤，維持系統的穩定性。由於這屬於核心層級的穩定性修復，建議所有使用 Linux 核心的系統管理員應立即更新至修補後的核心版本，以防止潛在的系統崩潰風險。由於原文未提供具體的受影響版本或CVSS分數，修補建議為更新核心。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "watchdog", "rzv2h", "除零錯誤", "系統穩定性"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Fixes Watchdog: rzv2h Avoids Division-by-Zero Error, Preventing System Crashes",
    summary_en: "This announcement details a vulnerability found in the Linux kernel's watchdog: rzv2h. The root cause of this vulnerability is that the clk_get_rate() function may return 0. If this value is not properly handled, it can lead to a division-by-zero operation, subsequently causing a system crash (panic). This patch aims to ensure that the system safely avoids the division-by-zero error when clk_get_rate() might return 0, thereby maintaining system stability. Since this is a core-level stability fix, all system administrators using the Linux kernel are advised to immediately update to the patched kernel version to prevent potential system crash risks. As the original text did not provide specific affected versions or CVSS scores, the patch recommendation is to update the kernel.",
