    title: "Linux 核心漏洞修復：da9063 驅動程式在系統暫停/恢復時的 watchdog 處理問題",
    summary: "本漏洞涉及 Linux 核心中的 watchdog 機制，特別是針對 da9063 驅動程式的處理邏輯。當驅動程式在 `da9063_wdt_probe()` 中設定了 `WDOG_HW_RUNNING` 狀態，但使用者空間（userspace）未開啟設備時，`WDOG_ACTIVE` 狀態會保持清除。這導致在執行 `da9063_wdt_suspend()` 時，`wdt_disable()` 函式不會被執行。結果，在系統進入暫停（suspend）狀態時，watchdog 計時器會持續計數，最終引發系統意外重置（unexpected system reset）。修復建議是檢查 `WDOG_HW_RUNNING` 和 `wdd` 相關邏輯，以確保在系統暫停流程中正確地停用 watchdog，避免誤觸系統重置。建議系統維護者應更新到修復此問題的 Linux 核心版本。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "watchdog", "da9063", "系統重置", "suspend/resume"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Vulnerability Fix: Watchdog Handling Issue in da9063 Driver During System Suspend/Resume",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability involves the watchdog mechanism within the Linux kernel, specifically concerning the handling logic for the da9063 driver. When the driver sets the `WDOG_HW_RUNNING` state in `da9063_wdt_probe()`, but the device is not active in userspace, the `WDOG_ACTIVE` state remains cleared. This results in the `wdt_disable()` function not being executed when `da9063_wdt_suspend()` is called. Consequently, the watchdog timer continues to count when the system enters a suspend state, eventually triggering an unexpected system reset. The suggested fix is to review the `WDOG_HW_RUNNING` and `wdd` related logic to ensure the watchdog is correctly disabled during the system suspend process, preventing accidental system resets. System maintainers are advised to update to the Linux kernel version that addresses this issue.",
