    id: "20261014-16172",
    trackers: ["os", "security"],
    category: "Linux",
    title: "Linux 核心修復 pwrseq_device_register() 函數的 NULL 指標解引用漏洞",
    summary: "本漏洞存在於 Linux 核心的電源序列化（power sequencing）機制中，具體影響 `pwrseq_device_register()` 函數。當 `dev_set_name()` 呼叫失敗時，程式會跳轉至 `err_put_pwrseq` 標籤。然而，`pwrseq_release()` 函數會無條件地嘗試迭代 `targets` 列表，並進而解引用一個無效的指標，導致潛在的 NULL 指標解引用（NULL-pointer dereference）錯誤。修復建議是將對 `dev_set_name()` 的呼叫，移到 `targets` 列表頭初始化之後，以確保在釋放資源時，相關指標的有效性。此修復屬於核心元件層面的安全修正，旨在提高系統穩定性和安全性。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "pwrseq_device_register", "NULL-pointer dereference", "核心漏洞", "Linux 安全更新"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Fix Addresses NULL Pointer Dereference Vulnerability in pwrseq_device_register() Function",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability resides within the Linux kernel's power sequencing mechanism, specifically affecting the `pwrseq_device_register()` function. When `dev_set_name()` fails, the program jumps to the `err_put_pwrseq` label. However, the `pwrseq_release()` function unconditionally attempts to iterate through the `targets` list, subsequently dereferencing an invalid pointer, which leads to a potential NULL pointer dereference error. The suggested fix is to move the call to `dev_set_name()` to after the initialization of the `targets` list, ensuring the validity of related pointers during resource release. This patch constitutes a core component security fix aimed at enhancing system stability and security.",
    tags_en: ["Linux Kernel", "pwrseq_device_register", "NULL-pointer dereference", "Kernel Vulnerability", "Linux Security Update"],
    sources: [
      { name: "NVD CVE API", url: "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98411", lang: "EN" }
    ]
