    title: "研究人員利用 OpenAI GPT-5.6 模型，在六天內成功鏈接 Google Chrome 三個漏洞，實現遠端代碼執行",
    summary: "資安公司 XBOW 的研究團隊展示了一種極具威脅性的攻擊鏈，該鏈利用了三個先前未公開的 Google Chrome 漏洞，在使用者僅載入網頁的情況下，即可在 Windows 系統上執行代碼。這項攻擊鏈成功跨越了 Chrome 的多層沙盒保護機制。Google 已確認並修補了所有三個漏洞，並向 XBOW 支付了 250,000 美元的獎勵。攻擊鏈的建立過程展示了 AI 代理（AI agents）的巨大影響：XBOW 利用 GPT-5.6 等公開模型，在六天內完成了原本需要專業團隊數月甚至數年才能完成的複雜漏洞鏈。這三個漏洞分別位於 Chrome 的 JavaScript 引擎、WebP 圖片解析程式碼，以及 Crashpad 崩潰處理器。雖然所有漏洞已修補，但此事件凸顯了 AI 工具加速漏洞挖掘和攻擊鏈構建的潛在風險，並大幅降低了攻擊的門檻。",
    tags: ["Google Chrome", "XBOW", "GPT-5.6", "漏洞鏈", "Windows", "遠端代碼執行"],
    title_en: "Researchers Use OpenAI GPT-5.6 Model to Chain Three Google Chrome Vulnerabilities and Achieve Remote Code Execution",
    summary_en: "The research team from cybersecurity firm XBOW demonstrated a highly threatening attack chain that leveraged three previously undisclosed Google Chrome vulnerabilities. This chain allows code execution on Windows systems merely by loading a webpage. The attack chain successfully bypassed Chrome's multi-layered sandbox protection mechanisms. Google has confirmed and patched all three vulnerabilities, paying XBOW a $250,000 bounty. The process of building the attack chain highlighted the significant impact of AI agents: XBOW utilized public models like GPT-5.6 to complete a complex vulnerability chain in six days—a task that would typically require a professional team months or even years. The three vulnerabilities were located in Chrome's JavaScript engine, the WebP image parser, and the Crashpad crash handler. Although all vulnerabilities have been patched, this incident underscores the potential risk of AI tools accelerating vulnerability discovery and attack chain construction, significantly lowering the barrier to entry for attackers.",
    tags_en: ["Google Chrome", "XBOW", "GPT-5.6", "Vulnerability Chain", "Windows", "Remote Code Execution"],
    sources: [
      { name: "The Hacker News", url: "https://thehackernews.com/2026/10/researchers-used-public-openai-model-to.html", lang: "EN" }
    ]
