    title: "Palo Alto Networks GlobalProtect™ 應用程式於 macOS 存在權限提升漏洞，可能讓一般使用者升級至 root 權限",
    summary: "Palo Alto Networks 的 GlobalProtect™ 應用程式在 macOS 作業系統上存在一個本地權限提升（local privilege escalation）漏洞。此漏洞允許未具備管理員權限的本地使用者，透過執行任意指令的方式，將其權限提升至 root 層級。這代表攻擊者無需管理員密碼，即可在受影響的 macOS 設備上執行高權限的惡意程式碼。然而，值得注意的是，GlobalProtect 應用程式在 Linux、Windows、iOS、Android 和 Chrome OS 等其他作業系統平台，並未受到此漏洞的影響。修補建議是使用者應立即更新 GlobalProtect 應用程式至最新版本，以修復此 macOS 上的安全漏洞。",
    tags: ["Palo Alto Networks", "GlobalProtect", "macOS", "權限提升", "CVE-2026-0315"],
    title_en: "Palo Alto Networks GlobalProtect™ application on macOS has privilege escalation vulnerability, potentially allowing standard users to escalate to root privileges",
    summary_en: "The GlobalProtect™ application from Palo Alto Networks contains a local privilege escalation vulnerability on the macOS operating system. This vulnerability allows a local user without administrator privileges to escalate their permissions to the root level by executing arbitrary commands. This means an attacker can execute high-privilege malicious code on an affected macOS device without needing an administrator password. However, it is worth noting that the GlobalProtect application is not affected by this vulnerability on other operating system platforms such as Linux, Windows, iOS, Android, and Chrome OS. The recommended remediation is for users to immediately update the GlobalProtect application to the latest version to patch this macOS security vulnerability.",
