    trackers: ["os"],
    category: "重點關注",
    title: "WhatsApp推出「訪客通話」功能，讓無帳號用戶也能參與加密語音與視訊通話",
    summary: "WhatsApp宣布推出「訪客通話」（guest calling）功能，允許用戶邀請任何沒有WhatsApp帳號的人加入群組或一對一通話。此功能旨在擴大通訊圈層，讓更多人能參與端到端加密的語音和視訊通話。根據說明，訪客在進入通話前會進入等候室，且必須經過主機（host）的批准才能加入。訪客的權限受到限制，無法看到其他參與者的電話號碼、發送訊息或邀請其他人。該功能支援螢幕分享、舉手和表情符號反應等功能，且訪客可以直接透過電腦瀏覽器加入，無需安裝App。此外，WhatsApp還宣布正在開發與Google Calendar和Outlook的整合，未來將允許用戶直接從日曆創建通話連結。此舉顯示WhatsApp正積極擴展其通訊服務的邊界，使其能更方便地與外部用戶進行加密通訊。",
    tags: ["WhatsApp", "訪客通話", "端到端加密", "Google Calendar", "Outlook"],
    title_en: "WhatsApp Launches 'Guest Calling' Feature, Allowing Non-Account Users to Join Encrypted Voice and Video Calls",
    summary_en: "WhatsApp has announced the 'Guest Calling' feature, which allows users to invite individuals who do not have a WhatsApp account to join group or one-on-one calls. This feature aims to expand its communication reach, enabling more people to participate in end-to-end encrypted voice and video calls. According to the description, guests will enter a waiting room before joining the call and must be approved by the host. Guest permissions are restricted; they cannot see the phone numbers of other participants, send messages, or invite others. The feature supports functions such as screen sharing, raising hands, and emoji reactions, and guests can join directly via a computer browser without needing to install the App. Furthermore, WhatsApp announced it is developing integrations with Google Calendar and Outlook, which will eventually allow users to create call links directly from their calendar. This move demonstrates WhatsApp's active effort to expand the boundaries of its communication services, making it easier to conduct encrypted communication with external users.",
    tags_en: ["WhatsApp", "Guest Calling", "End-to-End Encryption", "Google Calendar", "Outlook"],
