    title_en: "AI Sphera Launches AITEM: AI-Driven Threat Exposure Management Platform Revolutionizes Security Operations and Attack Surface Management",
    summary_en: "AI Sphera unveiled its AI-driven Threat Exposure Management (TEM) platform, AITEM, at GovWare 2026 in Singapore, showcasing the latest trends in automating security operations using Artificial Intelligence (AI). The speaker emphasized that while traditional Attack Surface Management (ASM) tools can provide asset inventories and vulnerability information, subsequent processes like impact investigation and departmental confirmation still require manual human handling. This creates an asymmetry between defensive response and attack speed. AITEM aims to solve this problem by organically linking multi-stage security operations processes, such as processing natural language business requests, asset information investigations, and new vulnerability impact confirmation. Specific applications include: handling natural language queries like, 'Which vulnerabilities disclosed this week affect our organization'; and utilizing an AI Agent to integrate internal tools like Slack, Confluence, and Jira to track the owner of unmanaged external exposed servers and analyze their business context. However, the speaker also stressed that while AI can handle repetitive investigative work, the entity responsible for the final decision on risk acceptability and response priority must remain human security personnel, necessitating a collaborative model between AI-assisted investigation and human-led advanced threat hunting.",
